1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Welcome to KNULL Queue Destroyer.
In this quick setup, we will go from install to first session.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
We will also cover Discord monitoring and optional IMAP verification setup.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Open the latest release in the public releases repo.
Download the Windows setup executable or macOS DMG.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Install the app, then launch it.
Use the latest release unless you were told to use a rollback build.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:49,000
On first launch, enter your activation key.
Use a user key. Admin keys are not valid on this client activation screen.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:03,000
After activation, open Proxy Pool.
Add proxies and run health checks to confirm usable endpoints.

7
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Keep healthy proxies active.
Remove dead or unstable proxies before live runs.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Next, open Accounts and add your account entries.
Configure account-level proxy behavior where needed.

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Open Profiles and create a reusable session profile
for viewport and browser behavior.

10
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Go to Task Groups and create your first group.
Set retailer, URL, instance count, proxy group, and optional account assignment.

11
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:10,000
For Walmart flows, account assignment influences
effective instance behavior.

12
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Open Sessions and launch one test session.
Confirm that it starts correctly and remains stable.

13
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:35,000
If launch fails, open Logs immediately.
Logs are the fastest way to identify the exact cause.

14
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Now open Discord Monitor and configure channel monitoring.
Tune cadence and cooldown to avoid duplicate trigger storms.

15
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Validate your monitor in a low-risk channel first,
then scale to production channels.

16
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Optional step: open Settings and configure IMAP polling.
This enables verification code detection and possible session injection.

17
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Once your setup is stable,
export a config backup from Settings.

18
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Keep your build updated to the latest release
for fixes and workflow improvements.

19
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:58,000
You now have a complete baseline setup.
Thanks for watching.
